    "updated_at": "2026-06-10T21:50:47Z",
    "body": "The reason that its a div is because I reused the element from appearance:auto, which [happens to be a div](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/forms/menu_list_inner_element.h;l=12;drc=c9ded7f18331563286e950c8867d670eb677e225).\n\nChanging it to be inline for base appearance would be very easy and is probably fine. Removing the element entirely by just making it a text node child of the button slot would be more challenging to implement, and I wonder if it would break the `gap:0.5em` we put on the select element to separate this text element from `::picker-icon`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
