    "created_at": "2026-06-11T18:36:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-11T18:36:38Z",
    "body": "> I wonder if it would break the gap:0.5em\n\nOnly if the author also add `display: content` to `::picker-icon`.\n\n`display: content` also fixes the baseline alignment in the empty string case,\n**+1 to `display: content` on the fallback element.**\n\n(Using `display: content` on pseudo-elements like `::picker-icon` feels like undefined behavior anyway, so hopefully authors don't do that.)\n\nhere what it should looks like with `display: content` on the fallback element **(2.)**,\nhttps://codepen.io/sb3nder/pen/EaZyWJw\nchrome:\n\n<img width=\"1015\" height=\"852\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/38db47ae-893e-4f3f-8302-deefccba339b\" />\n\nfirefox:\n\n<img width=\"601\" height=\"262\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/44a39ca2-ee7d-414c-982a-6416afbb7c79\" />",
    "author_association": "NONE",
